# 🗄️ AETHERIA — DATABASE SYSTEM

> **The Database System is the persistent memory of Aetheria.**
>
> The Game State System determines what has changed.
>
> The Database System stores those changes.

---

# 📌 1. OVERVIEW

The **Database System** is responsible for storing, retrieving, and maintaining persistent data used by the Aetheria game.

The Database System stores information generated and modified by other systems, especially the:

```text
GAME STATE SYSTEM
```

The Database System does **not** determine how the world behaves.

Instead:

```text
GAME STATE SYSTEM
        ↓
determines state changes
        ↓
DATABASE SYSTEM
        ↓
stores updated data
```

This separation allows Aetheria to maintain a clean architecture between:

```text
GAME LOGIC
GAME STATE
DATA STORAGE
```

---

# 🧠 2. CORE PRINCIPLE

The most important principle is:

> **The Game State System controls state. The Database System stores state.**

Example:

```text
Before:

Village Population = 100
```

A Cult attack occurs.

The Game State System calculates:

```text
Population - 30
```

Result:

```text
New Population = 70
```

Then:

```text
GAME STATE SYSTEM
        ↓
Village Population = 70
        ↓
DATABASE SYSTEM
        ↓
Save Population = 70
```

The Database does not decide:

```text
Population - 30
```

That decision belongs to the Game State System.

