# ⚡ 36. TRANSACTION SYSTEM

When one action modifies multiple databases, the update should be treated as one logical transaction.

Example:

```text
HERO RECRUITED
```

The action may require:

```text
Character Database
Inventory Database
Master Database
Recruit Database
Collection Database
Event Database
```

Transaction:

```text
BEGIN TRANSACTION
        │
        ├── Create Hero
        ├── Deduct Currency
        ├── Update Collection
        ├── Update Recruit State
        └── Update Master State
        │
        ▼
COMMIT
```

If something fails:

```text
ROLLBACK
```

This prevents partially saved actions.

